---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Fidelic — a fake Salesforce org that breaks on command';
const description =
  "Fidelic is a 14MB Docker container that loads your real org's schema, runs your real Apex triggers, and injects failures you can't test anywhere else — row locks, rate limits, tenant throttling.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>You can't test API limits without taking down Salesforce for your whole company.</h1>
  <p class="sub">
    Row locks, rate limits, tenant-wide throttling — untestable in any sandbox, at any
    price.
  </p>

  <p class="answer">
    Fidelic is a fake Salesforce org in a 14MB Docker container. Boots in 2 seconds.
    Loads your real org's schema and runs your real Apex triggers. Breaks on command.
  </p>

  {/* TODO: when async ships (C2 recorded-effects / inline-after-commit), swap the
      CaseTrigger REFUSED row for "≈ SIMULATED  CaseTrigger  EventBus.publish → captured,
      not sent" demonstrating inline-after-commit. Until recorded-effects is BUILT it must
      read REFUSED — provable-claims rule (no advertising unbuilt behavior). */}
  <div class="terminal" role="img" aria-label="Terminal: Fidelic boots, classifies each trigger as executed or refused with a reason, then returns an UNABLE_TO_LOCK_ROW error when failure injection is enabled.">
<pre><span class="cmd">docker run -p 8080:8080 fidelic/emulator --apex-src ./force-app</span>
<span class="dim">fidelic v1.0  ·  booted in 1.9s  ·  image 14 MB</span>

<span class="dim">classifying triggers against your org schema …</span>
  <span class="ok">✓ EXECUTE</span>     AccountTrigger          before/after insert, update
  <span class="ok">✓ EXECUTE</span>     ContactTrigger          after insert
  <span class="bad">✗ REFUSED</span>     CaseTrigger             EventBus.publish — not yet simulated
  <span class="bad">✗ REFUSED</span>     BillingSync.trigger:88  dynamic SOQL — not in the subset

<span class="cmd">export SFEMU_FAULT_LOCK_ON_UPDATE=true</span>   <span class="dim"># break it on command</span>
<span class="cmd">curl -sX PATCH $ORG/services/data/v62.0/sobjects/Account/001xx0000…</span>
<span class="bad">&#123; "errorCode": "UNABLE_TO_LOCK_ROW",</span>
<span class="bad">  "message": "unable to obtain exclusive access to this record" &#125;</span></pre>
  </div>

  <div class="receipts">
    <p>Verified 68/68 against a public conformance suite written from Salesforce's own docs.</p>
    <p><a href="#">Run the scorecard yourself →</a></p>
  </div>

  <blockquote class="pullquote">
    <p>
      The failure injection alone is worth it — row locks and API limits are untestable
      in any real org. Fidelic makes them a config flag.
    </p>
    <cite>— Engineer at a major Salesforce partner</cite>
  </blockquote>

  <div class="waitlist" id="waitlist">
    <h2>Early access</h2>
    <p>We're onboarding teams a few at a time. Leave an email; we'll reach out.</p>
    <form action="https://formspree.io/f/your-form-id" method="POST">
      <input
        type="email"
        name="email"
        placeholder="you@company.com"
        aria-label="Email address"
        required
      />
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Fidelic early access" />
      <button class="btn" type="submit">Get early access</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</Base>
